{"TOCTOU race condition in CreateOrUpdateDevice: device limit enforcement uses separate SELECT COUNT and INSERT/UPDATE operations without transaction or atomic guard, allowing concurrent requests to bypass the configured device limit": 0.8843094706535339, "Anonymous Authenticate returns error when device limit reached instead of continuing authentication, causing anonymous requests to fail entirely when limit is hit - behavioral change from previous implementation that logged but didn't block": 0.6510299444198608, "Type mismatch between frontend and backend: TypeScript declares anonymousDeviceLimit as number | undefined, but Go DTO uses plain int64 that serializes to 0 when unset, causing potential misinterpretation of 0 as 'no devices allowed' vs 'unlimited'": 0.411364883184433, "Layering violation: auth client (client.go) imports concrete anonstore package to check ErrDeviceLimitReached error, coupling auth layer to storage implementation details instead of depending only on anonymous.Service interface": 0.39938491582870483, "ProvideAnonymousDeviceService now constructs concrete AnonDBStore internally (accepting db.DB instead of AnonStore), breaking dependency inversion and testability": 0.36293745040893555, "TagDevice changed from async/fire-and-forget to synchronous execution, causing errors to bubble up to Authenticate and potentially blocking auth": 0.8862844705581665}